From 9d87cfdc98dd71ba20cbeff0732ffd73fca4adc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:18:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Talk T5a: the generator engine talk_gen.c and the grammar
 compiler talkc_gen.py

The generator writes a resident's line only from the database: template
strings chosen by a guarded, weighted grammar (TB_GRAMMAR, TB_STRINGS) and
concept forms. A line is [opener] [core] [callback] [tag] [hand-off]; the
core answers the act replied to with a reply act core/data/talk/acts.tsv
allows; fillers ({x} the topic with its forms and fields, the speaker's
likes and job, names, the catchphrase), sub-rules, the story's line codes
and faces. Guards over the room, the speaker's persona, mood, relationship
and stage, the facts (callbacks read from the sim's accessors), the topic.
Cast lines weigh 8x; novelty rings per speaker and per room; re-picks, the
bubble and a 3-sentence cap, then dropped parts, then a safe line; an
alternative whose filling fails is set aside; a per-conversation RNG.

Safety: talk_gen_exchange runs talk_safe_gate first (K-7 ends the talk),
every line goes through talk_safe_lint (a hit plays a safe line, counts
and logs), a filler the room may not hear is never used, a typed name is
probed (talk_safe_lint_probe), romance replies need the gate's pass and
the target's consent, one everyday swear a conversation (K-9).

talkc_gen.py compiles grammar/<lang>/*.tlk and voice/<lang>/*.tlk and
refuses unknown guards and slots, illegal reply acts, hand-made articles,
lines that cannot fit, swears without blunt&adults_only, callbacks without
a fact, hate-list words, echoing refusals, guarded safe lines; 15 seeded
bad grammars. test_talk_gen.c: 13 engine tests on core/tests/talk_gen/.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
