+# core/data/talk/acts.tsv - the discourse acts' adjacency table (owner: TK, T5a;
+# docs/TALK.md "The generator", design 3.1 and quality check Q2).
+#
+# ACT<TAB>CLASS<TAB>REPLIES
+#   ACT      a talk.h TA_* act without the prefix; every act has a row
+#   CLASS    open ask tell warm cool third flow romance gesture safety (talk.h TAC_*:
+#            the openers are chosen by the class of the act they answer)
+#   REPLIES  the acts a resident's line may perform in answer (comma separated).
+#            The first is the default reply act of a core.<act> rule with no
+#            `act:`. talkc refuses a core.<ACT> rule whose reply act is not here,
+#            and a react.<R> rule is only used after a line R may answer.
+# A reaction (one resident to another) answers the previous LINE's act, so
+# the reply acts have rows too.
+
+GREET	open	GREET,ASK_FEELING,JOKE,TELL,COMPLAIN,BACKCHANNEL,TEASE
+FAREWELL	open	FAREWELL,PROMISE,JOKE,COMPLAIN,TEASE
+THANK	open	ANSWER,JOKE,TEASE,BACKCHANNEL,DISMISS
+APOLOGIZE	open	ANSWER,DISMISS,JOKE,COMPLAIN,COMFORT
+INTRODUCE	open	GREET,ASK_ABOUT,JOKE,TEASE
+ASK_ABOUT	ask	ANSWER,OPINE_POS,OPINE_NEG,TELL,JOKE,CHANGE_TOPIC,DISMISS
+ASK_OPINION	ask	OPINE_POS,OPINE_NEG,ANSWER,JOKE,CHANGE_TOPIC,DISMISS
+ASK_FEELING	ask	ANSWER,TELL,COMPLAIN,JOKE,DISMISS
+ASK_FACT	ask	YES,NO,ANSWER,JOKE,DISMISS
+ASK_WHO	ask	GOSSIP,ANSWER,DISMISS,JOKE
+ASK_ADVICE	ask	ANSWER,ENCOURAGE,JOKE,DISMISS
+ASK_FAVOR	ask	YES,NO,OFFER,COMPLAIN,JOKE
+ASK_REPEAT	ask	ANSWER,COMPLAIN,JOKE
+TELL	tell	BACKCHANNEL,ASK_ABOUT,OPINE_POS,OPINE_NEG,JOKE,AGREE,TEASE,CONTINUE,LAUGH
+OPINE_POS	tell	AGREE,DISAGREE,OPINE_POS,OPINE_NEG,JOKE,TEASE,LAUGH,BACKCHANNEL
+OPINE_NEG	tell	AGREE,DISAGREE,OPINE_POS,OPINE_NEG,JOKE,TEASE,SYMPATHIZE,BACKCHANNEL,LAUGH
+AGREE	tell	AGREE,BACKCHANNEL,JOKE,LAUGH,TELL,TEASE
+DISAGREE	tell	DISAGREE,AGREE,JOKE,TEASE,OPINE_POS,OPINE_NEG,DISMISS,COMPLAIN,LAUGH
+ANSWER	tell	BACKCHANNEL,AGREE,ASK_ABOUT,JOKE,TELL,TEASE,LAUGH,DISAGREE
