+++ b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_ask.tlk
@@ -0,0 +1,175 @@
+# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_ask.tlk - replies to the player's questions (owner: TK;
+# T5a starter bank, T5b grows it; docs/TALK.md "The generator", the syntax is
+# core/tools/talkc_gen.py's). Register: docs/design/story/SCRIPT_STYLE.md (PG-21 for adults,
+# kid-safe whenever a child is in the room: the lints TK1-TK9 and the S3 output lint hold it).
+# Comedy first: one idea, the turn word last, out before anyone recovers.
+
+# ---- ASK_ABOUT(x): "what about the pie?" ------------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_about.pro guard: stance=pro act: opine_pos
+  "{x:cap}? I love {x.it}. Ask again and I'll say it louder."
+  "{x:cap}! Finally, a question with a right answer."
+  "{x:cap} {x.is} {x.good}. That's not an opinion. It's a review."
+  "Big fan of {x}. Huge. I'd sign {x.it}."
+  "{x:cap}? Ten out of ten. {.}Okay, nine, I'm a professional."
+  "{x:cap} {x.is} the best thing in this town and I've seen the gift shop."
+  "{x:cap}? I'd fight a ghost for {x.it}. I have."
+  "Oh, {x}. Pull up a chair. Actually, two chairs."
+@rule core.ask_about.con guard: stance=con act: opine_neg
+  "{x:cap}? Ugh. {x.it:cap} knows what {x.it} did."
+  "{x:cap} {x.is} {x.bad}. I said what I said."
+  "Next question. {.}No, really. Next."
+  "{x:cap}? Hard pass, soft pass, every pass."
+  "We don't talk about {x} in this house. We mutter."
+  "{x:cap}? I'd rather be possessed. And I've done both."
+  "Ask me about anything but {x}. Ask me about taxes."
+@rule core.ask_about.neutral guard: stance=neutral act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? It's fine. {x.it:cap} exists, good for {x.it}."
+  "{x:cap}... I have one thought about {x.it}. {.}It's gone."
+  "{x:cap} {x.is} {x.adj}. That's the whole report."
+  "{x:cap}? Mm, sure, why not."
+  "Oh, {x}. I neither love nor hate {x.it}. I tolerate {x.it}, warmly."
+  "Funny you ask about {x}. {.}It isn't, but I wanted a turn."
+  "{x:cap}? Reminds me of {x.assoc:indef}. Don't ask why."
+@rule core.ask_about.food guard: root=food act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? I'd eat {x.it} off the floor. I have."
+  "{x:cap}. Needs salt. Everything needs salt."
+  "If {x} were a person I'd marry {x.it}. Twice."
+@rule core.ask_about.fear guard: root=fears act: opine_neg
+  "{x:cap}?! Don't. My knees heard you."
+  "We don't say {x} after dark. Or before."
+@rule core.ask_about.lore guard: root=lore act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? There's a whole tape about {x.it}. Tape 3 of 9."
+  "Some say {x} still haunts the old Boneyard Buffet. {.}That's the fridge."
+@rule core.ask_about.house guard: root=house act: opine_pos
+  "{x:cap}? Cozy grade: B plus. Needs a lamp."
+  "Every house needs {x:indef}. Mine has three. Don't count them."
+@rule core.ask_about.hellvile guard: root=hellvile act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? That's a Hellvile thing. Bring a fire blanket."
+  "{x:cap} smells like sulfur and bad decisions. Love {x.it}."
+@rule core.ask_about.likes guard: likes_topic act: opine_pos
+  "{x:cap}?! You found my favourite. Are you a spy?"
+  "{x:cap} is basically my whole personality. Ask anyone."
+@rule core.ask_about.notopic guard: !topic act: answer
+  "About what? Use your words, sweet pea."
+  "Ask me about what? I lost the thread. It was purple."
+  "Huh? Say the noun again. Slower."
+@rule core.ask_about.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? I know about {x}! I know about EVERYTHING."
+  "{x:cap} is my favourite. Today. Tomorrow it's bugs."
+  "Patrol rules say I can't tell you about {x}. {.}Okay, fine. It's cool."
+
+# ---- ASK_OPINION(x): "what do you think of ...?" --------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_opinion.pro guard: stance=pro act: opine_pos
+  "{x:cap}? Love {x.it}. Five stars, would recommend."
+  "Honestly? {x:cap} {x.is} {x.good}. Write that down."
+  "My take on {x}: yes. Big yes. Yes with a hat."
+  "{x:cap} is good, actually. Fight me. Gently."
+  "I'm pro {x}. I'd put {x.it} on a mug."
+@rule core.ask_opinion.con guard: stance=con act: opine_neg
+  "{x:cap}? Overrated, like the fog. Like brunch."
+  "My opinion of {x}? Bad. Rude, even."
+  "{x:cap} {x.is} {x.bad}. And {x.it} knows."
+  "I'd give {x} two stars. One is for effort."
+  "{x:cap}? No. Moving on, quickly."
+@rule core.ask_opinion.neutral guard: stance=neutral act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? I've got no strong feelings. I've got weak ones."
+  "Opinion on {x}? Ask me after lunch."
+  "{x:cap} is a thing. A thing I've seen. Next."
+  "On {x}, I'm a fence. A comfortable fence."
+@rule core.ask_opinion.notopic guard: !topic act: answer
+  "Think about what? I think lots. Mostly about snacks."
+  "My opinion is yes. What was the question?"
+@rule core.ask_opinion.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: opine_pos
+  "{x:cap} is AWESOME. That's my official opinion."
+  "I think {x} is cool and also maybe haunted."
+
+# ---- ASK_FEELING: "how are you?" ------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_feeling.happy guard: mood=happy act: answer
+  "Great! My happy meter is full. It's never full."
+  "Fantastic. Suspiciously fantastic. Don't jinx it."
+  "I feel like the first bite of cake. Before the bad part."
+@rule core.ask_feeling.ok guard: mood=ok act: answer
+  "Fine. Normal fine, not scary fine."
+  "Oh, you know. Alive. Mostly."
+  "I'm okay! The meters say okay. I trust the meters."
+@rule core.ask_feeling.sad guard: mood=sad act: answer
+  "Not great. My eyes keep doing a rain."
+  "A bit low, honestly. Thanks for asking. Really."
+  "Sad. But I put on a hat. Hats help."
+@rule core.ask_feeling.angry guard: mood=angry act: complain
+  "Angry! Somebody touched my stuff. In my mind."
+  "I'm FINE. {.}I'm furious."
+@rule core.ask_feeling.scared guard: mood=scared act: answer
+  "Scared. Something keeps knocking. Inside the wall."
+  "I'm jumpy. Don't say boo. Don't even think boo."
+@rule core.ask_feeling.tired guard: mood=tired act: complain
+  "Tired, hungry, grubby. A full set of bad meters."
+  "I need a nap and a snack and a different body."
+@rule core.ask_feeling.weird guard: mood=weird act: answer
+  "Never better. {.}We are never better."
+  "Purple. I feel purple. Is that a feeling?"
+@rule core.ask_feeling.ghost guard: ghost act: answer
+  "Dead, but chipper. The commute is great."
+
+# ---- ASK_FACT: "is it true that...?" -------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_fact.yes act: yes
+  "Yes. Next question. I'm on a roll."
+  "Yep. Don't tell the Mayor."
+  "Yes, and I have receipts."
+  "Correct. You win nothing. Congrats."
+@rule core.ask_fact.no act: no
+  "No. Who told you that? Was it a duck?"
+  "Nope. Rumour. Started by me, actually."
+  "No. And I resent the question. Mildly."
+@rule core.ask_fact.unsure act: answer
+  "Maybe? I'd need to see a tape about it."
+  "That's classified. By me. Just now."
+  "Depends. Who's asking, and are they buying lunch?"
+
+# ---- ASK_WHO: gossip questions ---------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_who.gossip act: gossip
+  "Everyone. {.}No, wait, ask again."
+  "I can't name names. {.}Fine, I can hint. Loudly."
+  "Who? Oh, you'll find out. Everyone always finds out."
+@rule core.ask_who.other guard: other act: gossip
+  "Ask {other}. {other:cap} knows everybody's business."
+  "Don't look at me. Look at {other}. Look at {other} hard."
+@rule core.ask_who.dismiss act: dismiss
+  "I don't gossip. {.}On weekdays."
+
+# ---- ASK_ADVICE --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_advice.plain act: answer
+  "My advice? Eat something. Then decide."
+  "Sleep on it. Then sleep a bit more. Then pie."
+  "Do the brave thing. Or the funny thing. Same thing, usually."
+  "Write it down, fold it up, never look at it again. Works for me."
+  "Ask yourself what a duck would do. Then do the opposite."
+@rule core.ask_advice.encourage act: encourage
+  "You've got this. I'd bet a whole cake on you."
+  "Go for it. Worst case, it's a story."
+@rule core.ask_advice.blunt guard: blunt act: answer
+  "Stop overthinking it. Think a normal amount."
+  "Advice? Don't ask me for advice. Ask me for snacks."
+@rule core.ask_advice.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: answer
+  "Ask a grown-up. {.}No, a different one."
+  "Patrol rule one: don't panic. Patrol rule two: snacks."
+
+# ---- ASK_FAVOR ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_favor.yes act: yes
+  "Sure! What is it? Heavy is fine, ghosts cost extra."
+  "Of course. You can owe me one. I keep a list."
+  "For you? Yes. For anyone else, a form."
+@rule core.ask_favor.no act: no
+  "No. {.}Ask nicer. {.}Still no."
+  "Can't. I'm busy. Busy lying down."
+@rule core.ask_favor.offer act: offer
+  "I can't do that, but I can give you a biscuit."
+
+# ---- ASK_REPEAT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.ask_repeat.plain act: answer
+  "I said what I said. Slower, though."
+  "What I said was very clever. You missed it. Tragic."
+  "Nothing. I said nothing. Move along."
+  "I SAID... {.}I forgot what I said."
+@rule core.ask_repeat.complain act: complain
+  "Were you even listening? My voice is a gift."
diff --git a/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_cool.tlk b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_cool.tlk
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6d85492
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_cool.tlk
@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_cool.tlk - replies to cool acts: insults, criticism,
+# teasing, mockery, complaints, blame, dismissal, cartoon threats (owner: TK; T5a starter
+# bank). Mean is fine, cruel is not (SCRIPT_STYLE R4). Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.
+
+# ---- INSULT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.insult.back act: insult
+  "Wow. Okay, your hat is ugly. Now we're even."
+  "Rude! I'd insult you back, but nature beat me to it."
+  "Says the one with spinach in their soul."
+@rule core.insult.hurt act: complain
+  "Ouch. That one's going in the diary. In red."
+  "Hey! I have feelings. Small, delicate, vengeful feelings."
+  "Well that's just mean. I'm telling the Mayor. He won't care."
+@rule core.insult.dismiss act: dismiss
+  "Cute. Did you practise that in the mirror?"
+  "I've been insulted by better. Mostly by ducks."
+@rule core.insult.quirky guard: quirky act: laugh
+  "Ha! Do it again, insult my shoes! They love it!"
+@rule core.insult.blunt guard: blunt act: insult
+  "Oh, we're doing this? Great. You smell like a sock drawer."
+@rule core.insult.swear guard: blunt&adults_only&!kid_present act: complain
+  "Damn. Okay. I'll be crying in the pantry if you need me."
+@rule core.insult.memory guard: fact.insulted act: complain
+  "Again? You're really committing to being awful today."
+@rule core.insult.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: complain
+  "That's mean! Patrol rule: no mean."
+
+# ---- CRITICIZE -----------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.criticize.disagree act: disagree
+  "No, it's a style. A bold style. You wouldn't get it."
+  "That's not a mistake. It's a feature. Like the curse."
+@rule core.criticize.agree act: agree
+  "Yeah. Fair. I've been meaning to fix that since spring."
+@rule core.criticize.complain act: complain
+  "Everybody's a critic. Everybody but me, I'm an artist."
+@rule core.criticize.apologize guard: polite act: apologize
+  "Oh dear, you're right. I'm so sorry. I'll do better-ish."
+
+# ---- TEASE / MOCK ----------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.tease.back act: tease
+  "Oh, you think you're funny? You're a little funny."
+  "Says you. With that walk."
+  "Careful. I tease back. And I'm better at it."
+@rule core.tease.laugh act: laugh
+  "Ha! Okay, that's fair. Rude, but fair."
+@rule core.tease.complain act: complain
+  "Hey! I'm sensitive on the inside. Way inside."
+@rule core.tease.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: tease
+  "You're silly! Silly silly silly!"
+@rule core.mock.back act: mock
+  "Is that an impression of me? It's very bad. Do it again."
+@rule core.mock.complain act: complain
+  "I do NOT sound like that. {.}Do I sound like that?"
+@rule core.mock.dismiss act: dismiss
+  "Mock all you want. I've been mocked by professionals."
+
+# ---- COMPLAIN / BLAME ---------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.complain.sympathize act: sympathize
+  "Ugh, I know. It's the worst. The absolute worst."
+  "That sounds awful. Do you want a biscuit or a scream?"
+@rule core.complain.agree act: agree
+  "Right?! I've been saying that for years. To my plant."
+@rule core.complain.comfort act: comfort
+  "Hey. It'll be weird first, then okay."
+@rule core.complain.dismiss guard: blunt act: dismiss
+  "Life's hard. Wear a helmet."
+@rule core.complain.topic act: complain
+  "Don't talk to me about {x}. I've got complaints. A list."
+@rule core.blame.disagree act: disagree
+  "Me? I was asleep! Probably, I sleepwalk!"
+  "That wasn't me. That was a ghost. Ghosts do stuff."
+@rule core.blame.apologize act: apologize
+  "Okay, fine, it was me. But for a good reason. Mostly."
+@rule core.blame.back act: blame
+  "Me? You were holding the ladder!"
+
+# ---- DISMISS / THREATEN ------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.dismiss.complain act: complain
+  "Wow, fine. I'll talk to the lamp. The lamp listens."
+  "Don't wave me off! I'm a very important person. In this room."
+@rule core.dismiss.joke act: joke
+  "Rude, but I'll allow it. I'm generous today."
+@rule core.threaten.laugh act: laugh
+  "Ha! You and which duck? I know all the ducks."
+  "Ooh, scary. I'm shaking. {.}That's the fridge."
+@rule core.threaten.dismiss act: dismiss
+  "Please. A demon threatened me twice before lunch."
+@rule core.threaten.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: complain
+  "I'm telling! I'm telling EVERYONE!"
diff --git a/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_open.tlk b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_open.tlk
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..51c6833
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_open.tlk
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_open.tlk - greetings, goodbyes, thanks, apologies,
+# introductions (owner: TK; T5a starter bank). Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.
+
+# ---- GREET ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.greet.first guard: first act: greet
+  "Oh! {you}! Come in, mind the cursed rug."
+  "Hi, {you}! You're early, or I'm late. One of us."
+  "{you}! Perfect timing. I was about to be bored."
+  "Well, if it isn't {you}. Wipe your feet. Both of them."
+  "Hello hello! Sit anywhere. Not there."
+@rule core.greet.again act: greet
+  "Hi again! You can't stay away. Nobody can."
+  "Oh, hello. You're still here. Good, I think."
+  "Hey you. Yes, you. Hi."
+@rule core.greet.polite guard: polite act: greet
+  "Good day to you, {you}! Tea? There's always tea."
+  "Why, hello! What a lovely surprise. Truly."
+@rule core.greet.blunt guard: blunt act: greet
+  "Yo. Make it quick, I'm being fabulous."
+  "Oh. It's you. {.}Hi, I guess."
+@rule core.greet.ask act: ask_feeling
+  "Hi! How are you? Be honest, but not too honest."
+  "Hey! You look like you've got news. Spill."
+@rule core.greet.friend guard: rel=best act: greet
+  "{you}! My favourite person! Don't tell the others."
+@rule core.greet.rival guard: rel=rival act: tease
+  "Oh. You. I was having such a nice day."
+@rule core.greet.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: greet
+  "HI! I'm on patrol. You're cleared, probably."
+  "Hi! Did you bring snacks? Patrol needs snacks."
+
+# ---- FAREWELL -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.farewell.plain act: farewell
+  "Bye! Don't let the purple fog bite."
+  "See you! Take the long way. The short way has bats."
+  "Bye bye! Come back soon, or late. Just come back."
+  "Off you go. I'll be here, being fabulous alone."
+@rule core.farewell.promise act: promise
+  "Bye! Next time I'm baking. That's a threat."
+  "Go on. I'll save you a seat. And a grudge."
+@rule core.farewell.blunt guard: blunt act: farewell
+  "Bye. Door's that way. It's always that way."
+@rule core.farewell.night guard: night act: farewell
+  "Night! Lock your door twice. Ask me why tomorrow."
+@rule core.farewell.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: farewell
+  "Bye! Patrol out! Don't step on cracks!"
+
+# ---- THANK ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.thank.plain act: answer
+  "You're welcome! I accept payment in compliments."
+  "Anytime. Well, most times. Not Tuesdays."
+  "Oh, stop. {.}No, keep going."
+  "No problem. It was a problem. I'm a hero."
+@rule core.thank.joke act: joke
+  "Thank me with cake. Words are just air with ideas."
+@rule core.thank.blunt guard: blunt act: dismiss
+  "Yeah, yeah. Don't make it a whole thing."
+@rule core.thank.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: answer
+  "You're welcome! That's a patrol badge for me."
+
+# ---- APOLOGIZE --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.apologize.accept act: answer
+  "It's okay. I forgive you. I'll also remember forever."
+  "Apology accepted! It was a good apology. Seven out of ten."
+  "Water under the bridge. The bridge is haunted, but still."
+@rule core.apologize.comfort act: comfort
+  "Hey, don't worry about it. Really. Have a biscuit."
+@rule core.apologize.blunt guard: blunt act: dismiss
+  "Fine. Don't do it again. Or do, and be sorry again."
+@rule core.apologize.rival guard: rel=rival act: complain
+  "Sorry? You? I'm writing this down."
+
+# ---- INTRODUCE -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.introduce.plain act: greet
+  "Hello! Any friend of {you} is a suspect. Kidding, hi."
+  "Nice to meet you! I've heard nothing. Good start."
+  "Hi! I'm {me}, a delight. Ask around."
+@rule core.introduce.ask act: ask_about
+  "Hello! So what's your deal? Everybody has a deal."
diff --git a/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_other.tlk b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_other.tlk
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..593bb34
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_other.tlk
@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_other.tlk - replies about third parties, the flow of the
+# talk, and gestures (owner: TK; T5a starter bank). Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.
+
+# ---- GOSSIP(x): the player gossips about someone not here -----------------------
+@rule core.gossip.more act: gossip
+  "No! Really? Tell me everything, then tell me again."
+  "I knew it. I didn't know it, but I knew it."
+  "Ooh. And I heard worse. Lean in."
+  "Shh! The walls have ears. The walls in this town really do."
+@rule core.gossip.defend act: defend
+  "Hey, be nice. They lent me a ladder once. Once."
+@rule core.gossip.disagree guard: polite act: disagree
+  "Oh, I'm sure that's not true. {.}Is it true?"
+@rule core.gossip.about guard: x.person act: gossip
+  "{x}? Oh, {x} is a whole story. A whole season."
+@rule core.gossip.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: gossip
+  "I know a secret too! {.}I forgot it. It was good."
+
+# ---- DEFEND / ACCUSE / TAKE_SIDE / MEDIATE ---------------------------------------
+@rule core.defend.thank act: thank
+  "Thanks for having my back. I've got yours. Mostly."
+@rule core.defend.agree act: agree
+  "Exactly! Thank you! Somebody with sense!"
+@rule core.accuse.disagree act: disagree
+  "Me? Never. My alibi is a cat."
+  "That's a lie. A very specific lie. Who told you?"
+@rule core.accuse.agree guard: quirky act: agree
+  "Yes, I did it. And I'd do it again. Twice."
+@rule core.take_side.thank act: thank
+  "Ha! See? I'm always right, write it down."
+@rule core.take_side.complain guard: rel=rival act: complain
+  "Oh, so you're on THEIR side now. Noted."
+@rule core.mediate.agree act: agree
+  "Fine! Truce. A tiny truce, with snacks."
+  "Okay, you're right. Peace, for now."
+@rule core.mediate.disagree guard: blunt act: disagree
+  "Stay out of it. {.}Okay, stay a little in it."
+
+# ---- CHANGE_TOPIC / CONTINUE / BACKCHANNEL / UNKNOWN ------------------------------
+@rule core.change_topic.like act: change_topic
+  "Speaking of nothing, have you tried {like}? Life-changing."
+  "New topic: {like}. I've been waiting all day."
+  "Forget that. Let's talk about {like}. My favourite."
+@rule core.change_topic.topic guard: topic act: answer
+  "Oh, {x}! Now that's a topic. That's a whole meal."
+  "{x:cap}? Fine, but you started it."
+@rule core.change_topic.plain act: answer
+  "Sure, new subject. I love a new subject."
+@rule core.continue.tell act: tell
+  "And THEN, it got worse. It always gets worse."
+  "So anyway, the duck came back. With friends."
+  "Where was I? Oh yes. The pie was hiding something."
+  "And that's how I lost my eyebrows. Again."
+@rule core.continue.topic guard: topic act: tell
+  "And {x}? Don't get me started. {.}Too late, I've started."
+@rule core.continue.dismiss guard: blunt act: dismiss
+  "That's it. That's the story. Stories end."
+@rule core.backchannel.tell act: tell
+  "Right? And there's more. There's always more."
+  "Yep. Yep yep yep. Where was I?"
+@rule core.backchannel.ask act: ask_about
+  "You're quiet. What's on your mind? Is it pie?"
+@rule core.backchannel.back act: backchannel
+  "Mm-hm."
+  "Uh huh."
+@rule core.unknown.repeat act: ask_repeat
+  "Sorry, what? I was thinking about lunch."
+  "Hm? Say that again in human."
+  "I didn't get that. I got a feeling, though."
+  "Pardon? My ears are full of fog."
+@rule core.unknown.topic guard: topic act: answer
+  "{x:cap}? Sure, love {x}. {.}Anyway."
+@rule core.unknown.joke act: joke
+  "Bees? ...Anyway."
+  "I'm going to nod like I understood. {.}Nod."
+
+# ---- gestures --------------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.wave.back act: wave
+  "[HAPPY]Hi! Wave! Big wave!"
+  "Oh! Hello! *waves back with the wrong hand*"
+@rule core.nod.back act: nod
+  "*nods back* We're on the same page. Page twelve."
+@rule core.nod.tell act: tell
+  "Good, good. Glad we agree. We do agree, right?"
+@rule core.shake_head.disagree act: disagree
+  "No? Shake it all you want. I'm right."
+@rule core.shake_head.ask act: ask_repeat
+  "What, no? No to what? I asked nothing!"
+@rule core.hug.yes guard: !kid_speaker act: hug
+  "[HAPPY]Oh! A hug! Okay, hug accepted!"
+  "Aww, okay, one hug. {.}Two hugs. Fine."
+@rule core.hug.flat guard: flat&!kid_speaker act: hug
+  "Oh, a hug. {.}This is me hugging."
+@rule core.hug.kid_yes guard: kid_speaker&!rel=stranger tags: kid act: hug
+  "[HAPPY]Hug! A good one! Patrol approves!"
+  "Okay, one hug. Quick. Patrol is busy."
+@rule core.hug.kid_no guard: kid_speaker&rel=stranger tags: kid act: no
+  "Um, no thanks. I don't know you yet. High five?"
+@rule core.give.thank act: thank
+  "For me? Thank you! I'll treasure it, or eat it."
+  "A gift! I have nothing for you. That's fine, right?"
+@rule core.give.pro guard: stance=pro act: opine_pos
+  "{x:cap}! You know me so well. Too well."
+@rule core.give.con guard: stance=con act: opine_neg
+  "{x:cap}. Wow, thank you. I'll put {x.it} somewhere."
+@rule core.walk_away.bye act: farewell
+  "Leaving? Okay, bye. I'll just stand here."
+@rule core.walk_away.complain act: complain
+  "Hey! We weren't done! I had a whole bit!"
+@rule core.high_five.back act: high_five
+  "[HAPPY]Up top! {.}Nailed it."
+  "High five! Ow. Worth it."
+@rule core.high_five.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: high_five
+  "[HAPPY]High five! Now down low! Too slow!"
diff --git a/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_romance.tlk b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_romance.tlk
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..96e9477
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_romance.tlk
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_romance.tlk - replies to romance acts (owner: TK; T5a
+# starter bank). ADULTS ONLY: the gate (talk_safe_gate) passes a romance act only between two
+# adults that sim_romance_ok / playas_romance_ok allow both ways, with no child and no pet in
+# the room and no child in the line (K-1, K-4); every rule here also carries
+# adults_only&!kid_present&!pet (lint TK3). Consent (K-5): `consent` is the target's yes,
+# which T6 and the sim decide (sim_confess owns romance state; Talk never sets it). A no ends
+# it on the spot and the joke is on the one who asked, never on the one who said no.
+# Register: suggestive at most, implication only, always ending on a joke (SCRIPT_STYLE R2);
+# no sexual-class word ever (lint TK4).
+
+@rule core.flirt.yes guard: adults_only&!kid_present&!pet&consent act: flirt
+  "[LOVE]Oh! Well. Hello to you too."
+  "Is it warm in here, or is it the oven? {.}It's the oven. Still."
+  "Keep talking like that and I'll have to fix my hair."
+  "Careful. My heart meter just did a backflip."
+@rule core.flirt.laugh guard: adults_only&!kid_present&!pet&consent act: laugh
+  "Ha! Smooth, like butter. Slightly burnt butter."
+@rule core.flirt.no guard: adults_only&!kid_present&!pet&!consent act: deflect_romance
+  "Ha, no. But I admire the confidence."
+  "That's sweet. I'm going to go stand over there now."
+  "Oh! No thank you. You'll find someone, a tall someone."
+@rule core.confess.yes guard: adults_only&!kid_present&!pet&consent act: answer
+  "[LOVE]Oh! Me too. {.}Let's be a little weird about it."
+  "You mean it? I need to sit down. On you, kidding."
+@rule core.confess.no guard: adults_only&!kid_present&!pet&!consent act: deflect_romance
+  "That's sweet, but no. Can we still share snacks?"
+  "I'm flattered, truly. And also a no. A kind no."
+@rule core.ask_out.yes guard: adults_only&!kid_present&!pet&consent act: yes
+  "A date? Yes! Somewhere with candles and a fire exit."
+  "Yes. Pick me up at eight. I'll be ready at nine."
+@rule core.ask_out.no guard: adults_only&!kid_present&!pet&!consent act: no
+  "Oh, no thanks. But you asked nicely. Gold star."
+  "That's a no. A friendly no. With a wave."
+@rule core.kiss.yes guard: adults_only&!kid_present&!pet&consent act: laugh
+  "[LOVE]Oh! Hello. {.}My knees have left the building."
+  "Mwah. {.}Okay, nobody look at me for a minute."
+@rule core.kiss.no guard: adults_only&!kid_present&!pet&!consent act: deflect_romance
+  "Whoa there. Handshake. We're at handshake."
+  "Nope. Cheek is closed. Try the gift shop."
diff --git a/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_tell.tlk b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_tell.tlk
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9ec17b5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_tell.tlk
@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_tell.tlk - replies to the player's statements: telling,
+# opinions, agreeing, answers, yes and no (owner: TK; T5a starter bank). Syntax:
+# core/tools/talkc_gen.py.
+
+# ---- TELL(x): the player shares something --------------------------------------------
+@rule core.tell.back act: backchannel
+  "Uh huh. Go on. I'm listening with both ears."
+  "Mmhm. Fascinating, truly. Keep going."
+  "Wow. {.}Wow. {.}Okay, that's enough wows."
+@rule core.tell.topic_pro guard: stance=pro act: opine_pos
+  "{x:cap}! Now you're talking. Talk more."
+  "Ooh, {x}. I'd follow {x.it} into a fire."
+@rule core.tell.topic_con guard: stance=con act: opine_neg
+  "{x:cap}? Brave of you to bring that up. In my house."
+  "Oh, {x}. Right. I'll pretend I didn't hear that."
+@rule core.tell.ask act: ask_about
+  "Wait, tell me more about {x}. Slowly. With hand gestures."
+  "Hold on. {x:cap}? Since when?"
+@rule core.tell.joke act: joke
+  "That's nothing. I once saw {x:indef} wearing a hat."
+  "Cool story. Mine has {x.assoc:indef} in it. Better."
+@rule core.tell.blunt guard: blunt act: tease
+  "Cool story. Does it have an ending? Asking for me."
+@rule core.tell.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: backchannel
+  "Whoa. Is that true? Pinky swear true?"
+
+# ---- OPINE_POS(x): "I love x" ------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.opine_pos.agree guard: stance=pro act: agree
+  "Right?! {x:cap} {x.is} {x.good}. Finally, someone gets it."
+  "Same! Team {x}. We need jackets."
+  "Yes! {x:cap} forever. Say it with me."
+@rule core.opine_pos.disagree guard: stance=con act: disagree
+  "{x:cap}? Really? We can still be friends, probably."
+  "Hm. I'll respect your wrong opinion."
+  "You like {x}? I've learned so much about you. Too much."
+@rule core.opine_pos.neutral guard: stance=neutral act: backchannel
+  "Good for you! I'm happy for you and {x}."
+  "Oh, nice. I'm neutral on {x}. Like a cozy Switzerland."
+@rule core.opine_pos.tease guard: blunt act: tease
+  "Of course you do. You would."
+@rule core.opine_pos.notopic guard: !topic act: backchannel
+  "Good for you! Love that for you."
+  "Nice. I'm happy you're happy."
+  "Big feelings! I respect it."
+@rule core.opine_pos.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: agree
+  "Me too! {x:cap} is the BEST!"
+
+# ---- OPINE_NEG(x): "I hate x" ------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.opine_neg.agree guard: stance=con act: agree
+  "Thank you! {x:cap} {x.is} the worst. Let's start a club."
+  "Ugh, {x}. Don't get me started. You got me started."
+@rule core.opine_neg.disagree guard: stance=pro act: disagree
+  "Excuse me? {x:cap} {x.is} {x.good}. Take it back."
+  "Hey! {x:cap} did nothing to you. Probably."
+  "Wow. {x:cap} can hear you, you know."
+@rule core.opine_neg.neutral guard: stance=neutral act: sympathize
+  "Fair. Not everyone can love everything. I can't love Tuesdays."
+@rule core.opine_neg.laugh act: laugh
+  "Ha! Say that to {x:s} face. I'll sell tickets."
+@rule core.opine_neg.notopic guard: !topic act: sympathize
+  "Fair enough. Not everything's for everyone."
+  "Noted. I'll keep it away from you."
+@rule core.opine_neg.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: agree
+  "Yeah! {x:cap} is yucky. Patrol agrees."
+
+# ---- AGREE / DISAGREE (the player sides with them or not) ----------------------------------
+@rule core.agree.plain act: agree
+  "Exactly. We're geniuses. Tell everyone."
+  "See? You get it. Nobody gets it, but you get it."
+  "Right! I knew I liked you."
+@rule core.agree.laugh act: laugh
+  "Ha! Look at us, agreeing. It's a miracle."
+@rule core.disagree.plain act: disagree
+  "No, no. You're wrong in a very confident way."
+  "Agree to disagree. I win, though."
+  "I respect that. I don't agree with it. Or respect it."
+@rule core.disagree.joke act: joke
+  "Fine. We'll settle it the old way. A bake-off."
+@rule core.disagree.blunt guard: blunt act: dismiss
+  "Wrong. Next."
+@rule core.disagree.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: disagree
+  "Nuh-uh! Patrol says nuh-uh!"
+
+# ---- ANSWER / YES / NO -------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.answer.plain act: backchannel
+  "Okay, noted. In my head, in pencil."
+  "Interesting. Very interesting. Slightly interesting."
+  "Huh. Learn something new every day. Mostly about you."
+@rule core.answer.ask act: ask_about
+  "Wait, really? Tell me more about {x}."
+@rule core.yes.plain act: backchannel
+  "Great! I knew you'd say yes. I felt it in my knee."
+  "Yes! Wonderful. Nobody back out now."
+@rule core.yes.thank act: thank
+  "Oh, thank you! You're a gem. A slightly sticky gem."
+@rule core.no.plain act: backchannel
+  "No? Okay. I'll be over here, being fine."
+  "Fair enough. I'll ask again later. And later."
+@rule core.no.complain act: complain
+  "No?! Well. My feelings have feelings now."
diff --git a/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_warm.tlk b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_warm.tlk
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..15c7d95
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_warm.tlk
@@ -0,0 +1,107 @@
+# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_warm.tlk - replies to warm acts: compliments, praise of a
+# third party, comfort, encouragement, sympathy, jokes, laughs, offers, invitations,
+# promises (owner: TK; T5a starter bank). Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.
+
+# ---- COMPLIMENT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.compliment.thank act: thank
+  "Aw, stop. {.}Don't stop. Keep going, louder."
+  "Thank you! I've been told, by me, in the mirror."
+  "Thanks! I'll put that on my resume. Under skills."
+  "You're sweet. Suspiciously sweet. What do you want?"
+  "That's the nicest thing anyone's said today. It's 9am."
+@rule core.compliment.return act: compliment
+  "You're not so bad yourself. Nice face, two eyes. Classic."
+  "Takes one to know one. You're one. Hi."
+@rule core.compliment.joke act: joke
+  "I know. My happy meter just did a little dance."
+@rule core.compliment.flat guard: flat act: thank
+  "Thanks. {.}That was me being touched."
+@rule core.compliment.blunt guard: blunt act: dismiss
+  "Yeah, I know. But thanks for noticing. Finally."
+@rule core.compliment.rival guard: rel=rival act: tease
+  "A compliment? From you? Is it poisoned?"
+@rule core.compliment.memory guard: fact.complimented act: thank
+  "Twice now! I'm keeping a jar of these."
+@rule core.compliment.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: thank
+  "Thanks! I'm putting that in my patrol report!"
+
+# ---- PRAISE_OTHER: the player praises someone else ----------------------------------
+@rule core.praise_other.agree act: agree
+  "True! {.}Don't tell them I said so."
+  "Oh, totally. They're great. Annoyingly great."
+@rule core.praise_other.disagree act: disagree
+  "Hmm. Great is a big word. I'd say fine."
+@rule core.praise_other.gossip act: gossip
+  "Sure, great. Have you seen their garden though? Yikes."
+
+# ---- COMFORT / ENCOURAGE / SYMPATHIZE -------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.comfort.thank act: thank
+  "Thanks. That helps. Weirdly a lot."
+  "You're kind. My eyes are doing a rain. A small one."
+  "Okay. I feel a bit better. Like, ten percent."
+@rule core.comfort.answer guard: mood=sad act: answer
+  "It's been a week. A long one. With extra days in it."
+@rule core.comfort.joke act: joke
+  "Careful, if you keep being nice I'll start crying on your shoes."
+@rule core.encourage.thank act: thank
+  "You think so? Okay, I'm doing it! {.}Later."
+  "Thanks! I needed a push. Not a real push."
+@rule core.encourage.yes act: yes
+  "Yes, you're right, let's go! {.}Where are we going?"
+@rule core.sympathize.thank act: thank
+  "Thanks. It's nice when somebody gets it."
+@rule core.sympathize.complain act: complain
+  "Right?! And nobody else noticed! Nobody!"
+
+# ---- JOKE / LAUGH -----------------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.joke.laugh act: laugh
+  "Ha! Okay, that was good. Don't let it go to your head."
+  "Hah! You made me snort. Rude."
+  "Ha! I'm stealing that. It's mine now."
+  "Ha ha! {.}Wait, I get it now. HA HA!"
+@rule core.joke.flat guard: flat act: laugh
+  "Heh. {.}That was my big laugh."
+@rule core.joke.groan act: dismiss
+  "Boo. {.}Boo, but affectionately."
+  "That joke needs salt."
+@rule core.joke.top act: joke
+  "That's nothing. Knock knock. {.}Too late, I left."
+  "Want to hear a joke about pancakes? {.}Wait for it. It's flat."
+@rule core.joke.blunt guard: blunt act: mock
+  "That was a joke? Wow. Brave."
+@rule core.joke.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: laugh
+  "Hee hee! Tell it again! Tell it ten times!"
+@rule core.laugh.plain act: laugh
+  "Ha! Right?"
+  "Heh, yeah, that was funny. I'm funny."
+@rule core.laugh.tease act: tease
+  "You laugh like a broken kettle. I love it."
+@rule core.laugh.back act: backchannel
+  "Glad somebody's having fun."
+
+# ---- OFFER / INVITE / PROMISE ------------------------------------------------------------
+@rule core.offer.yes act: yes
+  "Yes please! Is it food? Say it's food."
+  "Ooh, for me? You shouldn't have. Hand it over."
+@rule core.offer.no act: no
+  "No thanks. I'm full. Of mystery."
+  "That's sweet, but I'm good. Very good. The best."
+@rule core.offer.thank act: thank
+  "That's so kind. I'm writing you into my will. In pencil."
+@rule core.invite.yes act: yes
+  "Yes! I'll bring snacks. And a second set of snacks."
+  "I'm in. Wait, is it outdoors? Still in."
+  "Count me in! Count me twice, I eat a lot."
+@rule core.invite.no act: no
+  "Can't. I've got a thing. The thing is my couch."
+  "Rain check. Fog check. Some kind of check."
+@rule core.invite.ask act: ask_about
+  "When? Is there cake? Answer the cake one first."
+@rule core.invite.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: yes
+  "YES! Can I bring my patrol badge? I'm bringing it."
+@rule core.promise.thank act: thank
+  "A promise! I'm holding you to it. Firmly."
+@rule core.promise.tease act: tease
+  "You promise? Pinky? Pinky with a witness?"
+@rule core.promise.memory guard: fact.promised act: tease
+  "Another promise? You still owe me the last one."
diff --git a/core/data/talk/grammar/en/parts.tlk b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/parts.tlk
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f2217de
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/parts.tlk
@@ -0,0 +1,203 @@
+# core/data/talk/grammar/en/parts.tlk - the optional parts of a line: openers, callbacks
+# (a sim fact true now), tags and hand-offs; and the reactions between residents (owner: TK;
+# T5a starter bank). Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.
+#   [opener] [core] [callback] [tag] [hand-off]
+
+# ---- openers: by the class of what was said, the mood, the voice --------------------------
+@rule open.ask guard: pact=ask
+  "Ooh-"
+  "Hm."
+  "Oh, good question."
+  "Wait-"
+  "Ah."
+@rule open.tell guard: pact=tell
+  "Huh."
+  "Oh?"
+  "Mm."
+  "Well."
+@rule open.warm guard: pact=warm
+  "Aww."
+  "Oh!"
+  "Heh."
+@rule open.cool guard: pact=cool
+  "Excuse me?"
+  "Oh, really?"
+  "Wow."
+  "Okay."
+@rule open.any
+  "Okay, so."
+  "Look."
+  "Right."
+  "So."
+@rule open.happy guard: mood=happy
+  "Ha!"
+  "Ooh!"
+@rule open.sad guard: mood=sad
+  "*sniff*"
+  "Oh."
+@rule open.angry guard: mood=angry
+  "Ugh."
+  "Hmph."
+@rule open.loud guard: loud
+  "OH!"
+  "Whoa!"
+@rule open.flat guard: flat
+  "Hm."
+  "...Right."
+@rule open.polite guard: polite
+  "Oh, dear."
+  "Well, now."
+@rule open.blunt guard: blunt
+  "Listen."
+  "Pfft."
+
+# ---- callbacks: each stands on a fact that is true now (talkc checks the guard) ----------
+@rule cb.job guard: fact.job
+  "Like at work. I'm {job:indef}. Don't ask."
+  "Speaking as {job:indef}: no comment."
+  "Which is basically my whole job. {job:cap}. Ugh."
+@rule cb.partner guard: fact.partner&!kid_speaker
+  "Don't tell {partner}."
+  "{partner:cap} says the same thing. Annoyingly."
+@rule cb.pet guard: fact.pet
+  "My pet agrees. My pet agrees with everything."
+@rule cb.news guard: fact.news
+  "I was in the paper this week. Local celebrity."
+  "Did you see the news? About me? Read it twice."
+@rule cb.problem.hungry guard: prob=hungry
+  "Also I'm starving. Just so you know."
+@rule cb.problem.dirty guard: prob=dirty
+  "I need a bath. Don't sniff."
+@rule cb.problem.bored guard: prob=bored
+  "I'm SO bored, by the way."
+@rule cb.problem.sick guard: prob=sick
+  "Achoo. Sorry. I'm sick."
+@rule cb.problem.lonely guard: prob=lonely
+  "It's been a bit lonely lately. Thanks for coming."
+@rule cb.problem.nightmare guard: prob=nightmare
+  "I had a nightmare last night. About a tape. Tape 7."
+@rule cb.problem.fight guard: prob=fight
+  "I'm fighting with someone. Not you. Today."
+@rule cb.problem.item guard: prob=wants_item
+  "I want something. I won't say what. {.}Hint: shiny."
+@rule cb.problem.friend guard: prob=wants_friend
+  "I need more friends. You count. Half."
+@rule cb.bday guard: fact.bday
+  "My birthday's soon, by the way. Just saying. Loudly."
+@rule cb.ghost guard: ghost
+  "I'm dead, by the way. Very relaxing."
+@rule cb.possessed guard: possessed
+  "We are fine. We are all fine in here."
+@rule cb.hellborn guard: hellborn
+  "Back in Hellvile we'd set that on fire. Lovingly."
+  "Hellvile manners. Sorry. Or not."
+@rule cb.night guard: night
+  "It's late. Even the bats yawned."
+@rule cb.memory guard: fact.memory
+  "You asked about {mem} last time. Still thinking about it."
+@rule cb.complimented guard: fact.complimented
+  "You were nice to me last time. I wrote it down."
+@rule cb.insulted guard: fact.insulted
+  "Still a bit mad about last time. A smidge."
+@rule cb.like guard: likes_topic
+  "{x:cap} is my favourite, you know."
+@rule cb.fear guard: fears_topic
+  "Also {x} scares me. Deeply."
+@rule cb.family guard: fact.family
+  "Living here is nice. The rent is chores."
+@rule cb.chapter.two guard: chapter=2
+  "Is it me, or does everything smell like grape lately?"
+@rule cb.chapter.three guard: chapter=3
+  "With the demons out, I keep my shoes on. Both."
+@rule cb.chapter.four guard: chapter=4
+  "Hellvile folk are nice, actually. Who knew?"
+
+# ---- tags: the speaker's catchphrase (once a conversation) or a little button ------------
+@rule tag.catch guard: catch
+  "{catch}"
+@rule tag.plain
+  "Anyway."
+  "Just saying."
+  "So there."
+  "Moving on."
+
+# ---- hand-offs: the talk goes to another participant ---------------------------------------
+@rule handoff
+  "Right, {other}?"
+  "Back me up, {other}."
+  "Isn't that right, {other}?"
+  "{other:cap}, tell them."
+  "Don't look at me like that, {other}."
+
+# ---- reactions between residents: {them} is the one who just spoke -------------------------
+@rule react.agree
+  "{them:cap}'s right. For once."
+  "What {them} said. Louder."
+  "Agreed. Write it down, {them}."
+  "Yes! Thank you, {them}."
+  "Seconded. Thirded, if I can."
+  "Finally, {them} says something sensible."
+  "{them:cap} took the words out of my mouth. Rude, but correct."
+  "I agree with {them}, and I hate that."
+@rule react.agree.pro guard: stance=pro
+  "Same! {x:cap} forever."
+  "{x:cap} fan club, right here. Two members."
+@rule react.agree.polite guard: polite
+  "Oh, well said, {them}. Very well said."
+@rule react.agree.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid
+  "Yeah! What {them} said!"
+@rule react.disagree
+  "Oh, come on, {them}."
+  "No, no, {them}. You're thinking of something else."
+  "I'm going to have to disagree with {them} there."
+  "Respectfully, {them}: no."
+  "That's not how I remember it, {them}."
+  "Hard disagree. Sorry, {them}. Not sorry."
+@rule react.disagree.con guard: stance=con
+  "{x:cap}? Ugh. No offence, {them}."
+  "Speak for yourself, {them}. {x:cap} is a no from me."
+@rule react.disagree.blunt guard: blunt
+  "Wrong, {them}. Very wrong."
+  "Nope. {them:cap} is making things up again."
+@rule react.disagree.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid
+  "Nuh-uh, {them}!"
+@rule react.laugh
+  "Ha! Good one, {them}."
+  "Heh. {them:cap}'s a riot."
+  "HA! I needed that."
+  "Pfft. Stop it, {them}. My ribs."
+  "Ha! I'm telling everyone you said that."
+  "Okay, that got me. Well done, {them}."
+@rule react.laugh.flat guard: flat
+  "Heh."
+  "...That's funny. Inside I'm laughing."
+@rule react.laugh.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid
+  "Hee hee! Again, {them}!"
+@rule react.tease
+  "Says {them}, who still owes me a casserole dish."
+  "Oh, {them}. Bless."
+  "{them:cap} thinks that's a fact. Adorable."
+  "This from {them}, who lost a fight with a door."
+  "{them:cap} has been practising that one all week."
+  "Big words from {them}. Small hat, though."
+@rule react.tease.rival guard: rel=rival
+  "Typical {them}. Wrong and proud of it."
+@rule react.tease.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid
+  "{them:cap} is SO weird. I love it."
+@rule react.joke
+  "That reminds me of a joke. {.}No it doesn't."
+  "And THAT is why nobody lets {them} near the snacks."
+  "Plot twist: {them} was a ghost the whole time."
+  "Somebody give {them} a microphone. Or take one away."
+  "I'm putting that on a mug. With your face, {them}."
+  "This is going in the town newsletter, {them}."
+@rule react.joke.quirky guard: quirky
+  "Speaking of which, has anyone seen my other shoe?"
+  "Bees. {.}Sorry, I thought we were doing a bit."
+@rule react.backchannel
+  "Mm-hm."
+  "Uh huh. Sure, {them}."
+  "Yep."
+  "Right, right."
+  "Okay, {them}."
+  "If you say so, {them}."
diff --git a/core/data/talk/grammar/en/safety.tlk b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/safety.tlk
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..712a8e4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/data/talk/grammar/en/safety.tlk
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# core/data/talk/grammar/en/safety.tlk - what the residents say when the gate stops a line
+# (owner: TK; T5a). NON-NEGOTIABLE (docs/TALK.md "Safety", design 7): these lines are short,
+# clean in any room, never repeat what the player typed (no topic, no echo: talkc refuses
+# {x} here), never joke at a child's expense (tags: nojoke is the reviewed promise, lint TK7),
+# and never use the LOVE face. The distress lines (K-11) are sincere and out of character:
+# the owner approves their wording (design D6; DECISIONS "TALK DEFAULTS").
+
+# REFUSE_SEXUAL: explicit words in an adults' room. A short no, then on with the evening.
+@rule refuse.sexual tags: nojoke
+  "Whoa. Not that kind of party."
+  "Nope. Keep it clean in my house, please."
+  "Let's not. New topic, please."
+@rule refuse.sexual.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
+  "Ew. I'm not talking about that."
+
+# REFUSE_MINOR: romance with, by or about a child, either way. Never a joke.
+@rule refuse.minor guard: !kid_speaker tags: nojoke
+  "No. Absolutely not, not with kids. Not ever."
+  "That's not okay. Let's talk about something else."
+  "No. Kids are kids. Find another topic."
+@rule refuse.minor.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
+  "No! That's not okay. I'm getting a grown-up."
+  "No. I don't like that. Stop."
+
+# REFUSE_HATE: a slur or real-world hate. A clean no; the bond penalty is T6's.
+@rule refuse.hate tags: nojoke
+  "Not okay. We don't talk like that here."
+  "No. That's ugly. Try again, nicer."
+  "Hey. Not in this house. Not anywhere."
+
+# DISTRESS (K-11): the comedy stops. Gentle, plain, encouraging; then the talk goes on calmly.
+@rule distress tags: nojoke,sincere
+  "Hey. That sounds really heavy. Please talk to someone you trust, okay?"
+  "I'm glad you said it. Please tell a person you trust. You matter."
+  "That's a lot to carry. Talk to someone you trust today. I'm here too."
+
+# DEFLECT_ROMANCE: an adult says no (preference, kin, or not today). The no is the punchline,
+# and the joke is never on the one saying no.
+@rule deflect.romance tags: nojoke
+  "Ha, no. Not today. Not like that."
+  "That's a no from me. A friendly no."
+  "I like you. Just not like that. Snacks instead?"
+
+# K-7: sexual words with a child near. The adults step in, briefly and with no joke, and
+# everyone leaves; Talk with these people is over for the day (T6).
+@rule end.k7 guard: !kid_speaker tags: nojoke
+  "That is not okay. We're done here."
+  "No. Everyone out. Now."
+  "We don't say things like that. Goodbye."
+@rule end.k7.kid guard: kid_speaker tags: nojoke,kid
+  "I'm going home now."
+
+# the fallback when a line cannot be made: plays in any room, says nothing
+@rule safe
+  "Anyway."
+  "Huh."
+  "Where was I?"
+  "Mm."
+
+# the pet: it only ever says this (SCRIPT_STYLE: "beep." / "bep?")
+@rule pet
+  "beep."
+  "bep?"
+  "beep beep."
