Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Talk T5a: bounded copies without strncpy in talk_gen.c

The sanitizer build (SAN=1, -O2 with -fsanitize) turns
-Wstringop-truncation on for the four strncpy copies into a line,
a name and a catchphrase, and -Werror stops the build. A small
copy_cap() does the same bounded copy and always ends the string.
Same output (the smoke census is identical in both builds); talk_gen.c
.text +6 B Thumb, +44 B MIPS, -6 B SH4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
