From 6c3925df92b6dcfa3ed1e84e05489877d0e81c26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:56:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Talk K-10: grief is not a punchline (the sincere grief
 and comfort banks)

A grief or loss topic (the lexicon's new grief flag, TCF_GRIEF: grief,
mourning, condolences, loss, memorial, funeral) now takes the sincere
`grief` bank whatever the player's act (the safety acts keep their own
sincere banks): the core line alone, no opener, callback, tag or hand-off,
and a reply act the adjacency table allows. Another resident may add one
sincere `comfort` line; the pet stays quiet. A grief word is never filled
into any other line (an association, the talk memory callback). Death,
ghosts and graves stay joke material (SCRIPT_STYLE R6, design 3.6, K-10).

- talk.h: TCF_GRIEF, TCB_LOSS, TGE_GRIEF / TGE_COMFORT, the guard
  predicates x.grief and fact.loss, TALK_GRIEF_DAYS.
- talk_gen.c: the grief route in talk_gen_line, the comfort reaction (one
  at most), the act-adjacency filter for those banks, the loss fact from
  family_memorial* (a household member's death in the last 28 town days,
  not a move away) and the {lost} name slot.
- talkc_gen.py: grief / comfort rules need act: and tags: nojoke; no
  register word, sub-rule, catchphrase, LOVE face or [JMAT]; {lost} only
  there; the full bank must answer every non-safety act with a line that
  needs no guard but the act's own. talkc.py: the grief row flag (clean,
  any age, talkable only).
- grammar/en/grief.tlk: the starter sincere bank (50 lines, kid, elder,
  loss and cast variants).
- The census: the 6 grief topics join the grid, and QF_K10_GRIEF fails a
  grief topic answered with anything but a sincere core line, or a grief
  word in a line that is not sincere.
- Tests: talk_gen_grief (the engine on the test grammar),
  talk_gen_property_grief (every act x every grief topic x adults', kids'
  and pet rooms; the household loss named; death topics still joke; a
  remembered grief topic never in a joke), K-10 in the rooms property
  test, 5 seeded bad grammars and a bad lexicon flag.

